      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "HOW TO USE\n\n1. Load Image: pick your AI 'pixel art' (any size, e.g. 1024x1024).\n   Example input: example_workflows/unfake_example_input.jpg (copy it to ComfyUI/input).\n\n2. Unfake Pixel Art: set target_width / target_height to the resolution the art SHOULD have\n   (e.g. 32x32 sprite, 64x64 icon). Count the 'big pixels' across the image if unsure.\n   Set both to 0 to auto-detect the pixel size instead (works best on clean, integer upscales).\n\n3. Tweak:\n   - max_colors: palette size (8-16 for sprites). 0 = keep all.\n   - remove_background + background_tolerance: raise tolerance (20-40) if bits of background remain.\n   - downscale_method: 'dominant' for noisy / JPEG images, 'nearest' for clean ones.\n   - fit_mode: what to do when the aspect ratio differs from the target (crop / pad / stretch).\n\nOutputs: pixel_art_image = real-size PNG (with alpha), upscaled_image = big crisp version, mask = transparency, manifest = JSON with the detected grid and palette."
      ],
